    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10b-2002-p10.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since the roots are \\(a\\) and \\(b,\\) Vieta’s formulas give \\(a + b = -a\\) and \\(ab = b.\\)\n\nFrom \\(ab = b\\) with \\(b \\ne 0,\\) we get \\(a = 1.\\) Then \\(a + b = -a\\) gives \\(1 + b = -1,\\) so \\(b = -2.\\)\n\nThus \\((a, b) = (1, -2),\\) and the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "By Vieta’s formulas, the sum of the roots is \\(-a\\) and the product is \\(b\\)",
        "So \\(a + b = -a\\) and \\(ab = b\\); use \\(b \\ne 0\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
